--TEST--
`goto` is refused at the keyword, and the diagnostic names the three shapes that replace it — a jump into the middle of a body has no edge in the control-flow graph the compiler builds
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `goto` is one of the PHP spellings the parser refuses outright, and the
// refusal lands on the keyword rather than on a label, so a file that never
// writes the label it names is refused just the same. `nvs-ir` leans on that:
// the statement roster in `lower/stmt.rs` guards this shape by `E0203`
// instead of lowering it.
int $n = 0;
if ($n == 0) {
    goto done;
}
echo $n, "\n";
// covers: lang:statements/statement-forms-that-do-not-parse
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0203]: `goto` is not supported
  --> case.nvs:9:5
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
